Fix missing location icons on the overhead/travel map in Rose Tattoo hires mode.

Root cause: TattooMap::drawMapIcons() paints each unlocked location's
icon (mapicons.vgs) directly into the map's own oversized (2x native),
persistent scrollable back buffer - it isn't a per-frame screen-space
overlay like most sprites, and the map's hires background override (see
rosetattoo-hires-map-upscale-override.patch) is likewise a persistent,
full-world buffer rather than something update() recomposites every
frame. Because of that, the existing queueRoseTattooHiresSprite() path
(used for e.g. inventory icons, see rosetattoo-hires-cursor-ai-override.
patch's sibling work) never gets a chance to run for map icons: nothing
ever re-queues them, so in hires mode they simply never appear on top of
the hires map background.

This patch adds Screen::paintRoseTattooHiresWorldSprite(), a sibling of
queueRoseTattooHiresSprite() that bakes an AI-upscaled true-color icon
override directly into the persistent _roseTattooHiresBackground buffer
at world/native coordinates (rather than the screen-space overlay layer),
and wires it into TattooMap::drawMapIcons() right after the existing
native low-res icon blit. Baking it into the world background means the
map's normal scroll-offset sampling in update() naturally keeps the icon
correctly positioned as the player scrolls the map, with no additional
per-frame bookkeeping - unlike the screen-space sprite layer, this only
needs to run once per icon, when the map is first shown.

Icon overrides reuse the frame-index-keyed lookup already implemented by
loadRoseTattooHiresCursorOverride() (frameIndex here is
MapEntry::_iconNum, mapicons.vgs's own frame index), so no new override
asset naming convention or extraction step is required - overrides are
expected at:
  $SCUMMVM_SHERLOCK_TATTOO_ASSET_OVERRIDES/sprites/mapicons_vgs/frame_NNN@Sx.png

